message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Incident Commander: an autonomous SRE agent that decides when not to act"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Shahesta
    family-names: Salama
    affiliation: Alryada University
  - given-names: Nourseen
    family-names: Tarek
    affiliation: Alryada University
repository-code: "https://github.com/S2800-0/incident-commander"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-10
keywords:
  - site reliability engineering
  - incident response
  - value of information
  - Bayesian inference
  - policy as code
  - Open Policy Agent
  - AI agents
abstract: >-
  A decision layer for incident response. Competing root-cause hypotheses are
  updated with Bayesian evidence, checks are chosen by value of information,
  every state-changing action is gated by an OPA policy engine outside the
  agent, only reversible actions run, and every decision is sealed in a
  Merkle tree signed with Ed25519 for offline verification.
